═══ STEP 147: Cosmic SFRD Correction at z > 6
    Quantifying the TEP isochrony-bias correction to the cosmic star formation rate density.

    ── Stage 1: Methodology ────────────────────────────────────
    If TEP inflates apparent stellar masses via isochrony bias, it also inflates
    apparent SFRs (since SFR is proportional to M* x sSFR in SED fitting).

    Correction formula: SFR_true = SFR_obs / Gamma_t^m
        SFR bias index m: 0.5000
      Rationale: UV-based SFR traces recent SF (< 100 Myr), less affected than cumulative mass
        Mass bias index n (for comparison): 0.7000
      LCDM reference: Mason+ 2015 / Bouwens+ 2022 extrapolation: log10(SFRD) = -1.5 - 0.35*(z-6)
        Redshift bins: z = 6-7, 7-8, 8-9, 9-10, 10-12
        Volume weighting: Flat LCDM comoving shell, H0=67.4, Om=0.315

